From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H. M. Yousuf <hmyousuf@nirapod.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:09:16 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: one CSDB for a run of protects

A protect is assembled as ORR followed by CSDB. When several protects
follow each other, the printer now emits the ORRs and a single CSDB after
the last one, provided that no ORR of the run reads a register written by
an earlier ORR of the run. The instructions moved before a CSDB are then
register-to-register ORRs, which neither access memory nor branch, and
every use of a protected value still comes after the CSDB. CSDB has no
architectural effect, so the printed code computes the same results as
the assembly program. A label or any other instruction ends a run.
